,121.48557,"","","","","","r","The grandest building on the Bund is now home to the Pudong Development Bank."],["Shanghai Gallery of Art","sight",31.23616,121.48655,"No. 3, Zhong Shan Dong Yi Road","Daily 10:00-19:00","","","","r","Recommended by Wikivoyage"],["Huangpu River ferry","activity",31.2346,121.48866,"","","","","","r","For those on a budget or short on time, you can take the ferry across to Pudong. This takes about 15 min and costs ¥2. One of the wharves is located at the Jinling East Road Zhongshan East 2nd Road crossing, as our map shows. Buy the…"],["City God Temple","sight",31.22778,121.48806,"249 Fangbang Zhong Lu","","","","","r","A well-known Taoist temple at the centre of the Old City, one of the biggest examples of traditional Chinese architecture in Shanghai. You can find local snacks and food as well as other traditional Chinese decorations in the…"],["Jiu Qu Qiao Bridge","sight",31.2284,121.48717,"","","","","","r","A zig-zagging bridge near the City God Temple, the present construction dates from the early 20th century."],["Yu Garden","sight",31.22917,121.4875,"29 Chenxiangge Lu","08:30-17:30","","","","r","A traditional Chinese Ming-style private garden that was built in 1559 but ransacked and restored several times since then. Entrance price is worth it for the many exquisite Chinese pavilions, seemingly never-ending paths, and sculpted…"],["Chenxiang Ge Temple","sight",31.22925,121.48559,"338 Fuyou Road","","","","","r","A historic Buddhist temple, with a statue on the upper floor carved from a rare wood."],["Baiyun Guan Temple","sight",31.2248,121.484,"239 Dajing Road","08:00-16:00","","","","r","A Taoist temple. Look for the statue of the guardian spirit for your Chinese zodiac."],["Xiaotayuan Mosque","sight",31.2207,121.48965,"Xiaotaoyuan Jie 52","","","","","r","A historic mosque that combines Chinese and Islamic architectural styles. Shanghai's largest mosque, with a separate women's mosque next door."]]}